PART 4: SERIALIZABLE isolation - expects SQLSTATE 40001
======================================================================
  Worker 1 result: ('40001 serialization_failure (40001)', None)
  Worker 2 result: ('settled', 50041)
  Under SERIALIZABLE isolation one worker commits and the other is
  aborted with SQLSTATE 40001 (serialization_failure) and must retry.

======================================================================
PART 5: READ COMMITTED vs REPEATABLE READ
======================================================================
  READ COMMITTED  reader saw: before=PENDING, after=SETTLED (sees the writer's commit)
  REPEATABLE READ reader saw: before=PENDING, after=PENDING (snapshot frozen at first read)

======================================================================
PART 6: Deadlock (40P01) and the fixed-account-order fix
======================================================================
  6a Buggy (lock in transfer direction):
    Worker 1: ('committed', 'RACE-DEAD-001')
    Worker 2: ('40P01 deadlock (DeadlockDetected)', 'RACE-DEAD-002')
    One worker should hit SQLSTATE 40P01 (deadlock_detected).
  6b Fixed (lock accounts in id order):
    Worker 1: ('committed', 'RACE-DEAD-001')
    Worker 2: ('committed', 'RACE-DEAD-002')
    Both workers commit; the lock-ordering prevents the deadlock.

